// Copy this file to Sentry.xcconfig and paste your DSN from
// Sentry → Project Settings → Client Keys (DSN).
//
// Sentry.xcconfig is gitignored. The DSN itself is a public client
// credential (it ships embedded in the app binary), but we don't
// commit it to keep the .example flow clean for forks.
//
// Write the DSN's "//" as "/$()/": an xcconfig reads "//" as the start of a
// comment, so a plain URL is cut to "https:". $() expands to nothing, so the
// app still gets https://... (Xcode Cloud: ci_scripts/ci_post_clone.sh does it).
//
// If Sentry isn't set up, the build still succeeds: crash reporting is off
// when SENTRY_DSN is empty.
SENTRY_DSN = https:/$()/examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
